<title>USA: Giscard d'Estaing says dlr-ffr level still welcome.</title>
<headline>Giscard d'Estaing says dlr-ffr level still welcome.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former French president Valery Giscard d'Estaing said Thursday the current dollar-franc level continued to be acceptable from the French point of view.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we are now in the target zone for us, so I'm not asking or wishing that there will be an additional change,&quot; Gicard d'Estaing said.</p>
<p>&quot;For us the present rate of exchange would be satisfactory,&quot; he told Reuters after giving a speech on European Monetary Union at Georgetown University.</p>
<p>The dollar-franc level stood at 5.7846 to the dollar at 2338 GMT Thursday.</p>
</text>
